course: dictionary
lesson: 7475
title: Portion, a part or share
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A portion is a part or share of something. It can also be the amount of food served to one person. «A large portion» means a big amount of food on your plate, and «portion size» means how much food you are given.
explain: «UK advice is at least 5 portions of fruit and veg a day.» Here a portion is one serving of fruit or vegetables, not a whole bag of apples. The clue is «at least 5 a day»: you count your portions, and you aim for five or more.
explain: To portion something out means to divide it into shares and give them out. Think of a parent sharing a cake between three children: they portion it out. Portion can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action), so look at the sentence to see which one it is.
fact: A portion is a part or share of something.
fact: A portion can also mean the amount of food served to one person.
fact: «Portion out» means to divide something into shares and give them out.
fact: «A child's portion is roughly what fits in their hand.» This is a helpful guide, not an exact measure.
fact: In Mandarin, fèn (falling tone) means portion, while fēn (high, level tone) means minute, so «shí fēnzhōng» means ten minutes.
exercise: «UK advice is at least 5 portions of fruit and veg a day.» In this sentence, what does portion mean? | A kind of fruit | *One serving of fruit or vegetables | A cup for drinking | A whole bag of apples
exercise: Mum says, «Please portion the cake out between the three of you.» What does portion out mean? | Eat it all yourself | Throw it away | Bake a bigger cake | *Divide it into shares and give them out
exercise: «A large portion of chips, please.» What does portion mean here? | A very small bite | A minute of time | *The amount of food served to one person | A kind of potato
test: In maths, what is «a portion of the cake»? | Crumbs left on the plate | The whole cake with no pieces cut | *A part or share of a whole | A sharp knife
test: Which word means a part or share of something? | porch | portrait | *portion | portal
exam: Read «She portioned the pizza into eight slices.» What kind of word is portioned here? | A full stop | A noun, naming a thing | An adjective, describing a thing | *A verb, showing an action
